<Layout title="Beyond Admissions" description="Wharton Chan's educational philosophy: guided exploration helps students understand their choices, discover their interests, and make decisions they can stand behind.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Admissions / The philosophy" title="Beyond Admissions" />
  <article class="container"><div class="prose"><p>Admissions is not just about getting into a good school. It is about learning how to choose.</p><p>Students are often asked to make life-shaping decisions before they have the vocabulary, exposure, or experience to understand the fields they are choosing between. Degrees sound similar. Careers blur together. School syllabi reveal very little of what disciplines actually involve.</p><p>My approach focuses on guided exploration — helping applicants understand the terrain before committing to a path. Through structured reading, discussion, and reflective work, students gain clarity about what genuinely interests them and why.</p><p>This process leads to stronger applications, but more importantly, to decisions applicants can stand behind.</p><p><strong>Admissions is a milestone. Learning how to choose is the education.</strong></p><a class="text-link" href="/admissions/book/">Begin a conversation <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13L13 3M3 3H13V13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" /></svg></a></div></article>
</Layout>
